If you send me a patch, issue, or pull request, you keep the credit for what
you wrote, and you give me a perpetual, worldwide, royalty-free, irrevocable
licence to use, change, and distribute it as part of the Work, under any
licence I choose. Do not send anything you do not have the right to share.


7. HOW TO GET PERMISSION

To do anything section 3 forbids, ask me first and get the answer in writing
(an email or a signed note is enough). Permission is for the specific thing I
agree to, it is not transferable, and I can set conditions such as credit
lines or non-commercial use only. Silence is never permission.

Contact: open an issue on the GitHub repository, or use the contact details
listed on my GitHub profile (github.com/Adityaadpandey).


